From 0f878dcb1b382078a852bf7eb35199034841bcdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhlport <nhlport@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:32:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] NHL 24: raise GfxEop on plain flips, flip back-pressure,
 stall diagnostics

- gnmdriver/liverpool: plain prepareFlip / prepareFlipLabel requests are patched
  into a new PatchedFlipEop NOP that raises GfxFlip and then GfxEop. Frostbite
  writes all of its GPU fences without interrupts and relies on the per-flip
  end-of-pipe interrupt that real hardware delivers to equeues registered with
  sceGnmAddEqEvent(kEqEventGfxEop); without it NHL 24's GfxEopEventLoop never
  woke up. sceGnmAddEqEvent now logs at Info.
- gnmdriver: ThrottleFlipSubmit holds sceGnmSubmitAndFlipCommandBuffers until
  the presenter is within 2 flips of the CPU (200 ms safety timeout), emulating
  real flip latency so the game's RenderLoop pacing (max 3 outstanding) holds.
- liverpool: SpinDiag warnings when a queue fiber spins > 2 s in WaitRegMem,
  Rewind or MemSemaphore (address, function, ref, mask, current value).
- equeue: infinite WaitForEvents reports every 5 s which queue/thread is stuck.
- videoout: LOG_DEBUG for submitted/presented flips.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
